#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186082919 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083390 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c6820924-ae0c-5bd0-b374-ef7b5badcc47" :knowledge-point/title "Creating a Venn Diagram Given a Description of a Sample Space"}] :question/id #uuid "6616ee7f-30ed-54ef-b578-b33bdb0101bf" :question/math-academy-id "e-13070" :question/problem "A dietician has $25$ patients, $10$ of whom are smokers, and $12$ of whom have diabetes. None of the diabetic patients are smokers. Represent the corresponding sample space using a Venn diagram." :question/worked-solution "Let us call $A$ the event \"The patient is a smoker\" and $B$ the event \"The patient has diabetes.\" \n\nSince none of the diabetic patients are smokers, we draw two non-overlapping circles to represent the events $A$ and $B.$\n\n- Since there are $10$ smokers, we write the number $10$ within the circle $A.$\n\n- Since there are $12$ patients with diabetes, we write the number $12$ within the circle $B.$\n\nThere are $25$ patients in total, so the number of remaining patients is \n\n$$\n25 - 10 - 12 = 3.\n$$\n\nTo represent the $3$ remaining patients, we write the number $3$ outside of the circles $A$ and $B.$\n\nFinally, our Venn diagram looks as follows:\n\n![](images/86/86855ecd3f1199c9a5c6fbb66ccf08d5b8dd2913d358f52d2c499039ea6fda4d.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186082920 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083391 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fbd8cd17-5aed-557e-b301-9828d84745c3" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Probability Using a Venn Diagram"}] :question/id #uuid "ad342550-d410-529f-a5c0-5b67845cff81" :question/math-academy-id "e-13071" :question/problem "The Venn diagram shown below represents two events $A$ and $B$ and the number of outcomes on each region of the sample space. Given that every outcome is equally likely, find $P(A\\cup B).$\n\n![](images/34/34ab66b54fcf6be9740be1fc89bd436ccc8d334dc8b20a5769993a93bd05b2f9.png)" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the probability of an event using a Venn diagram, we count the number of outcomes in the region that represents the event and divide by the total number of outcomes of the sample space $S.$\n\nIn the Venn diagram, $A\\cup B$ is represented by the area that is in either circle (see the illustration below).\n\n![](images/b2/b25a0b74f7b5242f783c38c81bdb4bf8025a847f7079fc90febe510fec041b6d.png)\n\nWe count up the outcomes:\n\n- The number of outcomes in $A \\cup B$ is\n\n$$\n20+15+25=60.\n$$\n\n- The total number of outcomes in $S$ is\n\n$$\n20+15+25+40=100.\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nP(A\\cup B)=\\dfrac{60}{100}= 0.6.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186082925 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083392 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c9401702-a2d9-5c53-a3de-8109a75111d7" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Probability Given a Description of a Sample Space"}] :question/id #uuid "fcdd0c3b-36f8-5452-820a-114a8e70aa49" :question/math-academy-id "e-13212" :question/problem "A survey conducted among $100$ students of a music school found that $68$ of them play piano, $39$ of them play violin, and there are $22$ students who play both instruments. Draw a Venn diagram representing this sample space. If a student is randomly selected among the $100$ students, what is the probability that they play at least one of these instruments?" :question/worked-solution "Let us call $A$ the event \"The student plays piano\" and $B$ the event \"The student plays violin.\"\n\nNote that there are $22$ students who play both piano and violin. We draw two overlapping circles representing the events $A$ and $B$ and write the number $22$ where the circles overlap.\n\n- The number of students who play *only* the piano is\n\n$$\n68 - 22 = 46,\n$$\n\nso we write the number $46$ in the part of circle $A$ that does not overlap with circle $B.$\n\n- The number of students who play *only* the violin is\n\n$$\n39 - 22 = 17,\n$$\n\nso we write the number $17$ in the part of the circle $B$ that does not overlap with circle $A.$\n\nThe total number of students who play at least one of the instruments is\n\n$$\n22+46+17 = 85,\n$$\n\nand there are $100$ students in total, so the number of remaining students is\n\n$$\n100 - 85 = 15.\n$$\n\nTo represent these $15$ students who play neither piano nor violin, we write the number $15$ outside of the circles $A$ and $B.$\n\nTherefore, our Venn diagram looks as shown below:\n\n![](images/cc/cc61c2a5c61467ac19d5debe2c2e53dc48f06f8d153c014f4a73e6feed514900.png)\n\nThe shaded part of the Venn diagram corresponds to students who play at least one of the instruments. The probability that a randomly selected student is from this group is given by\n\n$$\nP\\left(A\\cup B\\right)=\\dfrac{85}{100}= 0.85.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186559777 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083391 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fbd8cd17-5aed-557e-b301-9828d84745c3" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Probability Using a Venn Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09cc727b-a898-5540-97d6-f2c9b147974f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559035} {:answer/id #uuid "0b0f1776-a062-5fb8-a2c8-2000dc8577c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559039} {:answer/id #uuid "496c5835-4952-55d5-9f5b-9ea6b8e16eab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559206} {:answer/id #uuid "834552c3-6f8a-5fed-ba39-04a42ef90102" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.37" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559344} {:answer/id #uuid "e3d2cbdf-7de0-5fe4-813a-7b2573e8fd31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559578}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "09cc727b-a898-5540-97d6-f2c9b147974f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559035} :answer-field/id #uuid "332525cc-a511-5267-bb34-aaa17e24cd11" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559671}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0b138f98-60f4-5926-8616-f98d6e7b3754" :question/math-academy-id "q-11627" :question/problem "![](images/20/20aaaae06d88f9105276f77bb65975e7d775c8fd15fbf4984d9b1889e73503dd.png)\n\nThe Venn diagram above represents two events $A$ and $B$ and the number of outcomes in each region of the sample space. Given that every outcome is equally likely, find $P(A\\cap B)$ to $2$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "To calculate the probability of an event using a Venn diagram, we count the number of outcomes in the region that represents the event, and divide by the total number of outcomes of the sample space $S.$\n\nIn the Venn diagram, $A\\cap B$ is represented by the area that is inside the overlap between the circles (see the illustration below).\n\n![](images/c0/c0c7df273c9b71fc0286b03d7405cb8ca473d14b1020fc1ec15530879ddb8f1c.png)\n\nWe count up the outcomes:\n\n- The number of outcomes in $A\\cap B$ is $15.$\n\n- The total number of outcomes in $S$ is\n\n$$\n20+15+25+40=100.\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nP(A\\cap B)=\\frac{15}{100}=\\frac{3}{20}=0.15\n$$\n\nto $2$ decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186559837 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083392 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c9401702-a2d9-5c53-a3de-8109a75111d7" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Probability Given a Description of a Sample Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23feca0a-70cb-543d-b0d9-51f705b682a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.72" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559104} {:answer/id #uuid "297c5b88-2fb7-580a-8e17-ad860e113bd7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.85" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559120} {:answer/id #uuid "48fdc177-f885-5f30-a54e-78e80947ab4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.83" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559205} {:answer/id #uuid "97041577-9ffb-5796-9c28-3ac685cc9cb0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.76" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559395} {:answer/id #uuid "cb8c28da-829d-5a0f-bd54-32c167c55f41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.88" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559509}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cb8c28da-829d-5a0f-bd54-32c167c55f41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.88" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559509} :answer-field/id #uuid "ae364575-09e6-5cf9-9c82-8eb16e6ba56e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559738}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9ac83742-fbb3-5922-b2ad-70bce502b290" :question/math-academy-id "q-11631" :question/problem "At a band audition, there are $50$ singers. There are $27$ country singers, $23$ pop singers, and $6$ country and pop singers. Draw a Venn diagram representing this sample space. If a singer is selected at random among the $50$ singers, what is the probability that the singer sings country or pop music (or both)? Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Let us call $A$ the event \"the singer sings country music\" and $B$ the event \"the singer sings pop music.\"\n\nNote that there are $6$ singers singing both country and pop music. So, we draw two overlapping circles representing the events $A$ and $B$ and write the number $6$ where the circles overlap.\n\n- The number of singers who *only* sing country music is\n\n$$\n27-6=21,\n$$\n\nso we write the number $21$ in the part of circle $A$ that does not overlap with circle $B.$\n\n- The number of singers who *only* sing pop music is\n\n$$\n23-6=17,\n$$\n\nso we write the number $17$ in the part of circle $B$ that does not overlap with circle $A.$\n\nThe total number of singers who sing country or pop music is\n\n$$\n6+21+17=44,\n$$\n\nand there are $50$ singers in total, so the number of remaining singers is\n\n$$\n50-44=6.\n$$\n\nTo represent these $6$ singers who did not sing country or pop music, we write the number $6$ outside of the circles $A$ and $B.$\n\nTherefore, our Venn diagram looks as shown below:\n\n![](images/02/0240b83c3de5c8c3f3b1e91d3b9c8ae2899f0b2a18611d7e70b6dbf71f23e25b.png)\n\nThe shaded part of the Venn diagram corresponds to singers that sing country or pop music (or both). The probability that a randomly selected singer is from this group is given by\n\n$$\nP(A\\cup B)=\\frac{44}{50}=0.88.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186559854 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083391 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fbd8cd17-5aed-557e-b301-9828d84745c3" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Probability Using a Venn Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d507738-9fa2-5896-a470-f0b105f24c04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.43" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559045} {:answer/id #uuid "364cf66d-3412-5141-8d2d-02ccae075c69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.04" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559152} {:answer/id #uuid "6a78e3e7-3db8-5d5f-bc92-b9b93cb03eb0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.38" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559278} {:answer/id #uuid "8a94bf5f-4707-5650-aeb1-640b72693ca7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559364} {:answer/id #uuid "d25a2107-29ae-50bf-96cf-132fc63087e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.52" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559533}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8a94bf5f-4707-5650-aeb1-640b72693ca7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559364} :answer-field/id #uuid "2259f512-8e22-5ed6-bb49-42aefe325560" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559658}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c12c5e9b-72e8-5854-9bf8-a8cf7ba5e8c9" :question/math-academy-id "q-120043" :question/problem "![](images/c5/c5f197f52df26da43b27b2b142f25462570828996ea28154f865bac2e871e972.png)\n\nThe Venn diagram above represents two events $A$ and $B$ and the number of outcomes in each region of the sample space. Given that every outcome is equally likely, find $P(A\\cup B)$ to $2$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "To calculate the probability of an event using a Venn diagram, we count the number of outcomes in the region that represents the event, and divide by the total number of outcomes of the sample space $S.$\n\nIn the Venn diagram, $A\\cup B$ is represented by the area that is inside both circles (see the illustration below).\n\n![](images/ad/ad51768e560488687b0dfbd573f71136f7863106d0a830828878bc5488b05daf.png)\n\nWe count up the outcomes:\n\n- The number of outcomes in $A\\cup B$ is\n\n$$\n6+1+4=11.\n$$\n\n- The total number of outcomes in $S$ is\n\n$$\n6+1+4+12=23.\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nP(A\\cup B)=\\frac{11}{23}≈0.48\n$$\n\nto $2$ decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186559850 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083390 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c6820924-ae0c-5bd0-b374-ef7b5badcc47" :knowledge-point/title "Creating a Venn Diagram Given a Description of a Sample Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a1bdf2a-96e9-51d9-a76e-47feb46900c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/a5/a511835f1ecf6a7f3991f8ebb9ed14339ebfab4cb41aa06363502df5abf03719.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559122} {:answer/id #uuid "2d59aa09-be93-5eee-8d36-aa7f2a6de334" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/65/652f1e12bca4eaf43e7ad8d8c9de0a77f9d3f9904d84e10cd86a366ff7f4abaa.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559131} {:answer/id #uuid "8b1f0de5-0f2b-5045-865e-ad8049a87a40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/06/069844b0c1506a869fbefe3a0646416a5fa24b2eb9deecd819b0ff3bf60d55e2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559366} {:answer/id #uuid "ab239710-f6f9-5fa9-9991-5174c45175ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/7d/7d79399dfd4e3a0eedcccbfc878999e67c6998b4d500bdb30fecb8f9a805fd57.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559444} {:answer/id #uuid "f5a514d8-34b0-5fdf-afd1-074936c6ce73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/4c/4cd74e5a929964ad92259971a2b0cf83201e4d1ff912cb5d5d0880da1006a222.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559620}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2a1bdf2a-96e9-51d9-a76e-47feb46900c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/a5/a511835f1ecf6a7f3991f8ebb9ed14339ebfab4cb41aa06363502df5abf03719.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559122} :answer-field/id #uuid "a0501cb1-59d9-5e7f-87d0-8d8554465408" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559733}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b91a0507-397b-5914-a663-1432f07abc1f" :question/math-academy-id "q-121179" :question/problem "In a school, a survey conducted on the $40$ students shows that $17$ students traveled to school by train, $23$ students traveled by bus, and $10$ students traveled by both train and bus. \n\nIf $T$ represents the event that a student travels by train, and $B$ represents the event that a student travels by bus, which of the following diagrams gives the correct Venn diagram for the corresponding sample space?" :question/worked-solution "Note that there are $10$ students who traveled by both train and bus. We draw two overlapping circles representing the events $T$ and $B$ and write the number $10$ where the circles overlap.\n\n- The number of students who traveled by train *only*  is\n\n$$\n17-10=7,\n$$\n\nso we write the number $7$ in the part of circle $T$ that does not overlap with circle $B.$\n\n- The number of students who traveled by bus *only*  is\n\n$$\n23-10=13,\n$$\n\nso we write the number $13$ in the part of circle $B$ that does not overlap with circle $T.$\n\nThere are $40$ students in total, so the number of remaining students is \n\n$$\n40-7-10-13=10.\n$$\n\nTo represent the $10$ remaining students, we write the number $10$ outside of the circles $T$ and $B.$\n\nFinally, our Venn diagram looks as follows:\n\n![](images/a5/a511835f1ecf6a7f3991f8ebb9ed14339ebfab4cb41aa06363502df5abf03719.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186559860 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083392 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c9401702-a2d9-5c53-a3de-8109a75111d7" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Probability Given a Description of a Sample Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18daee96-9926-51bc-aa9c-54bcce231698" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.33" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559072} {:answer/id #uuid "2eba1f03-5431-549e-b34c-44334143652f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.67" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559134} {:answer/id #uuid "6833c09e-bc27-5478-af5c-17877146d61c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.37" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559276} {:answer/id #uuid "adf10555-c1f1-5075-9060-56b21226e412" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559454} {:answer/id #uuid "e154eea1-3d2f-5893-9370-222beb6bfa7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.54" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559573}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2eba1f03-5431-549e-b34c-44334143652f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.67" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559134} :answer-field/id #uuid "104a8090-a9a9-505d-bae0-c829e3a97494" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559648}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cc44bf24-a689-5cdc-ad9e-c41be1cff05a" :question/math-academy-id "q-121180" :question/problem "In a class of $30$ students, $18$ have black hair, $9$ have blue eyes and $7$ have both black hair and blue eyes. Draw a Venn diagram representing this sample space. If a student is selected at random among the $30$ students, what is the probability that the student has black hair or blue eyes? Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Let us call $A$ the event \"the student has black hair\" and $B$ the event \"the student has blue eyes.\"\n\nNote that there are $7$ students who have both black hair and blue eyes. So, we draw two overlapping circles representing the events $A$ and $B$ and write the number $7$ where the circles overlap.\n\n- The number of students who *only* have black hair is\n\n$$\n18-7=11,\n$$\n\nso we write the number $11$ in the part of circle $A$ that does not overlap with circle $B.$\n\n- The number of students who *only* have blue eyes is\n\n$$\n9-7=2,\n$$\n\nso we write the number $2$ in the part of circle $B$ that does not overlap with circle $A.$\n\nThere are $30$ students in total, so the number of remaining students is \n\n$$\n30-11-7-2=10.\n$$\n\nTo represent these $10$ students that have not black hair or blue eyes, we write the number $10$ outside of the circles $A$ and $B.$\n\nTherefore, our Venn diagram looks as shown below:\n\n![](images/fa/fab4a1a0244dc20c692101b35bac04ca9e73f4458a709d2507ba8d9a21345109.png)\n\nThe shaded part of the Venn diagram corresponds to students that have black hair or blue eyes. The probability that a randomly selected student is from this group is given by\n\n$$\nP(A\\cup B)=\\frac{11+7+2}{30}=\\frac{20}{30}≈0.67,\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083698 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083390 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c6820924-ae0c-5bd0-b374-ef7b5badcc47" :knowledge-point/title "Creating a Venn Diagram Given a Description of a Sample Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "95c48943-e8cf-52eb-8c3a-7075385c4728" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/72/72bc783c78e78798c87b8eee57ede740c8df18f0f6e83e0065497eedc2511a40.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186081120} {:answer/id #uuid "ee6e5fb5-b24b-5f6b-9344-3e008fe670ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/74/74aa1c8d177607476f6bc2f87eaf3b4020d797a47f8559744e3999820bc0aa90.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186081121} {:answer/id #uuid "fb13240a-7e95-58e7-be19-827e2f2083df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/3d/3da8b95c5182be1fd4c027e5e6f2ce84274286c805afdc84891bd5aecd14add9.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186081122} {:answer/id #uuid "fdbc6bae-4679-515d-b6ab-6d20fd308a16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/5c/5c2828cff69078cb82222b981b261010e2c0dc7f2f688945ded9a967402fa478.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186081123} {:answer/id #uuid "2cf145f5-c06d-551a-b6e2-efe50e6ef734" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/69/6938c3f414dc4fa9b110d0babae434ea8079f065d121c1710c6a7d91f10dafd9.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186081124}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fb13240a-7e95-58e7-be19-827e2f2083df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/3d/3da8b95c5182be1fd4c027e5e6f2ce84274286c805afdc84891bd5aecd14add9.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186081122} :answer-field/id #uuid "20fa1430-8dd3-5d74-994e-23d7c1d35350" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186081119}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "082ab98d-c2c3-56cd-8f7b-54c7956b64aa" :question/math-academy-id "q-42349" :question/problem "A language class has $63$ students, $43$ of them are studying English, and $25$ of them are studying Spanish. There are $10$ students studying both languages.\n\nIf $A$ represents the event that a student is studying English, and $B$ represents the event that a student is studying Spanish, which of the following gives the correct Venn diagram for the corresponding sample space?" :question/worked-solution "Note that there are $10$ students who study both languages. So, we draw two overlapping circles representing the events $A$ and $B$ and write the number $10$ where the circles overlap.\n\n- The number of students who *only* study English is\n\n$$\n43-10=33,\n$$\n\nso we write the number $33$ in the part of circle $A$ that does not overlap with circle $B.$\n\n- The number of students who *only* study Spanish is\n\n$$\n25-10=15,\n$$\n\nso we write the number $15$ in the part of circle $B$ that does not overlap with circle $A.$\n\nThere are $63$ students in total, so the number of remaining students is \n\n$$\n63-10-33-15=5.\n$$\n\nTo represent the $5$ remaining students, we write the number $5$ outside of the circles $A$ and $B.$\n\nFinally, our Venn diagram looks as follows:\n\n![](images/3d/3da8b95c5182be1fd4c027e5e6f2ce84274286c805afdc84891bd5aecd14add9.png)"}]}
